==Battleground==
*3 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 30~36.67 seconds<sup>900f~1,100f</sup>.
*8 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 12 seconds<sup>360f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*3 [[Pigeon de Sable]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Pterowl Hazuku]] spawns as the boss.
**8 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**8 [[Pigeon de Sable]]s spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
**1 [[Casaurian Ahirujo]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The strategy against Pterowl Hazuku is a bit different from [[Magma Tunnel Area 4]] this time. Since the boss wave triggers upon base hit, you will want to exhaust the other enemies first, especially the Wild Doges, since they both pose a threat and don't drop a lot of cash. [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] is good for this, as he is immune to the Waves produced by Pigeon de Sable and has [[Behemoth Slayer]] for the Wild Doges and won't over push like Courier Cat might. Be sure to build up your wallet and stack before hitting the base, because your main mission is to dispatch Casaurian Ahirujo as quickly as possible with [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Cutter Cat]] (if you have him). After that, [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] can tank all the enemies and hold the line comfortably, securing victory.

